	(text_box "PGOOD IS LEFT OPEN ON ALL THREE REGULATORS -- NOT AN OVERSIGHT\nPGOOD is open-drain and pulls LOW whenever its rail is down, which is precisely deep sleep. A 10k pull-up (the LM51571's recommended\nminimum) would sink 330 uA; even 100k sinks 33 uA continuously while asleep. No pull-up is fitted and no net is attached, so ERC\nreports these pins unconnected. No no-connect flags were added, on purpose: the ERC report is the reminder. If a rail-fault input is\never wanted, gate the pull-up -- do not just add one. U3 pin 15 (NC) is also left open.\nGND ON THIS SHEET IS BOARD GROUND. There is no GND_IN here; this sheet is downstream of the common-mode choke on power_input, so every\nground symbol is the board-side return. AGND (7), both PGND (1, 16) and the exposed pad (17) tie to that one net, so R10's 'resistor to\nAGND' lands on GND -- the same node. Star them properly in layout.\nVBAT appears as THREE hierarchical labels (U2 input, L3 input, U3 BIAS feed) rather than one dragged wire. Same name, same sheet, same\nnet -- confirmed in the exported netlist."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.0 114.86 0)
		(size 103.19 16.8)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0f7f8f6c-7e76-5f38-bbbd-5711c039ba59")
	)
	(text_box "2.2 MHz ON THE BOOST IS DELIBERATE: THE AM BROADCAST BAND IS 530 kHz - 1.7 MHz\nThis is a motorcycle. The boost is the loudest switcher on the board and it runs straight off the battery harness, which is the\nantenna. Its switching fundamental has to sit ABOVE the AM band, so U3 is set to 2.2 MHz -- the top of the LM51571-Q1's range and the\nfrequency its electrical table is characterised at (RT = 9.09k; equation 5: RT = 2.21e10 / fRT - 955). R11 = 37.4k also enables Dual\nRandom Spread Spectrum, whose low-frequency triangular profile targets exactly this band.\nThe two BUCKS CANNOT do the same thing: the LM5164's maximum switching frequency is 1 MHz, which is INSIDE the AM band. They are\ntherefore placed BELOW it -- R4 = 20.5k gives 402 kHz on the 3.3 V rail, R7 = 31.6k gives 396 kHz on the 5 V rail (FSW[kHz] = VOUT[V] x\n2500 / RRON[kohm]). Their fundamentals are clear of the band; harmonics 2 and 3 are not, and no LM5164 setting can fix that. Mitigate\nin layout and filtering, not by raising the frequency: keep both buck power loops tiny, and remember the common-mode choke on\npower_input is there for this noise."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.0 48.12 0)
		(size 103.19 16.8)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "641111d7-a762-507e-a57e-92f508f183fe")
	)
	(text_box "BEFORE THIS SHEET IS TURNED INTO A BOARD\n1. No footprints are assigned to anything here; the Footprint field is empty on all 42 parts. 2. The 'rails' sheet symbol in\nmccan.kicad_sch has NO sheet pins, so all seven hierarchical labels below raise hier_label_mismatch in ERC -- add pins VLOGIC_IN (in),\nVBAT (in), EN_3V3SW (in), EN_BOOST (in), +3V3_ALW (out), +5V (out), +24V (out). 3. There is still no PWR_FLAG in the project, so GND\nreports power_pin_not_driven. 4. Decide type-2 vs type-3 ripple injection for the two bucks and fit the parts. 5. Re-run U3's\ncompensation for 24 V. 6. Confirm the EN_BOOST pulldown exists on mcu_can and that nothing pulls EN_BOOST above 3.3 V. 7. L3 is 6.8 uH\nXAL4030-682ME -- check its saturation rating against the LM51571's 4.33 A switch current limit at the real 24 V load, not the nominal\none. 8. D4 SS5PH102 sees VOUT plus switch-node overshoot; verify its rating against the real layout's ringing and keep the D4 / C20-C22\n/ PGND loop as small as physically possible -- at 2.2 MHz that loop is the whole EMI story."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.0 133.16 0)
		(size 103.19 15.32)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "65b66702-6297-5b3e-bf8c-f5fecf23e5f2")
	)
	(text_box "WHERE EVERY VALUE CAME FROM\nU1 / U2 LM5164DDA, VREF = 1.200 V, RFB2 = 1.2 / (VOUT - 1.2) x RFB1 (eq 10): 348k/200k -> 3.288 V, 634k/200k -> 5.004 V, 6.0 uA each.\nTI recommends RFB1 in 100k..1M, so both sit inside the datasheet's own range. RRON: R4 20.5k -> 402 kHz, R7 31.6k -> 396 kHz; minimum\non-time at the worst case (VIN clamped to ~39 V by the input TVS) is 205 ns, well above the 50 ns floor. NOTE the LM5164 minimum VIN is\n6 V, so a deep crank dip drops both bucks out -- correct, but know it. C8 / C14 = 2.2 nF is MANDATORY and exact: the datasheet says a\nlarger bootstrap cap stresses the internal VCC regulator and damages the device. L4 / L5 = 22 uH gives 0.30 A (3.3 V) and 0.37 A (5 V)\nripple at 13.8 V in, 30-37% of the 1 A rating; pick a shielded part whose saturation current clears the LM5164's 1.5 A peak current\nlimit, not merely 1 A.\nU3 LM51571-Q1, VREF = 1.000 V, VLOAD = VREF x (RFBT/RFBB + 1) (eq 9): 115k/4.99k -> 24.05 V (+0.2%), 200 uA, drawn only while the boost\nis enabled. RT 9.09k -> 2.2 MHz. MODE 37.4k -> hiccup overload protection ON and spread spectrum ON (9.4.3). SS 22 nF, COMP 2.61k + 10\nnF, CHF 100 pF, VCC 5.1R + 1 uF, BIAS 0R + 100 nF are the datasheet's list-of-materials values for its 6-to-12 V / 1.6 A / 2.1 MHz\nboost example (table 10-2); the VCC 5.1R + 1 uF pair is a hard requirement of section 9.3.2, not a suggestion. THE COMPENSATION IS A\nSTARTING POINT, NOT A RESULT -- re-run R14 / C23 / C24 through the LM5157x Boost Quick Start Calculator for 24 V and this board's real\nload before a board spin.\nBIAS is fed from VBAT, not from +24V. Either is legal (BIAS operates 2.9 V to 45 V and the input TVS holds VBAT under that), but VBAT\nis unconditional whereas +24V only exists after the output pre-charges through L3 and D4. Shutdown current from BIAS is 2.6 uA typ / 5\nuA max and would be drawn through L3 + D4 from VBAT anyway, so moving it saves nothing. Count that 2.6 uA in the sleep budget."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.0 86.2 0)
		(size 103.19 27.16)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7bc8c910-6e2d-539c-9b76-33c6cc13177c")
	)
	(text_box "THE LM5164 IS A CONSTANT-ON-TIME REGULATOR -- IT NEEDS IN-PHASE RIPPLE AT FB TO BE STABLE\nCOT has no error amplifier. Datasheet 6.3.1 / table 6-1 require at least 20 mV of ripple at FB that is IN PHASE with the inductor\ncurrent. Ceramic output caps alone give capacitive ripple, 90 degrees out of phase; the classic failure is bursts of on-pulses followed\nby a long off-time. C9 / C15 are the type-2 feedforward caps the brief calls for -- they AC-couple output ripple to FB, but they do not\nby themselves make that ripple resistive. Finish it one of two ways before ordering boards.\n(a) TYPE 2, as drawn: add a small series resistance in the output-cap leg. Equation 4 gives RESR >= 20 mV / dIL, i.e. ~67 mohm (3.3 V\nrail, dIL 0.30 A) and ~54 mohm (5 V rail, dIL 0.37 A) at the 22 uH / 400 kHz operating point. Only ripple current flows in it (<1 mW)\nso it is nearly free, but it must be a real part -- do not rely on the cap's own ESR. (b) TYPE 3: the RA / CA / CB injection network of\nfigure 7-1 (453k / 3.3nF / 56pF in TI's 12 V design). That is what the EVM ships and it needs no series resistance at all.\nC9 / C15 = 100 pF is well above the equation-6 minimum (3.1 pF, 2.7 pF) and puts the coupling zero near 4.5 kHz, two decades below FSW,\nso the full output ripple reaches FB."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.0 66.42 0)
		(size 103.19 18.28)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "af66da9c-45e7-5195-afa5-91326de90272")
	)
	(text_box "SLEEP-BUDGET CRITICAL VALUES -- DO NOT \"TIDY\"\nBoth feedback dividers are >= 500 kohm on purpose. The LM5164's quoted quiescent\ncurrent does NOT include the external FB divider; a conventional 275 kohm divider\nwould add ~12 uA per rail, unbudgeted. At 348k/200k and 634k/200k each draws\n6.0 uA. A high-impedance FB node needs the feedforward cap for stability -- that\nis the trade being made deliberately.\nEN_UVLO_SYNC has NO divider. A line-UVLO divider there would draw ~14 uA\ncontinuously whether the boost is enabled or not. Driving it straight from the\nGPIO keeps \"floating = boost off\" via the EN_BOOST pulldown."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.0 13 0)
		(size 103.19 15.32)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d4edd780-00b9-5c1d-b3a0-1665cd681bc8")
	)
	(text_box "U3 PIN 6 (EN_UVLO_SYNC) IS DRIVEN DIRECTLY BY EN_BOOST.  THERE IS NO DIVIDER.  DO NOT ADD ONE.\nThe LM51571-Q1 typical application puts RUVLOT/RUVLOB from VSUPPLY to this pin to set a line UVLO. That divider sits across the battery\nrail and conducts whenever the battery is present, enabled or not -- about 14 uA, a large fraction of this board's whole deep-sleep\nbudget. It was removed on purpose: the MCU brown-out and the LM51571's own VCC UVLO (2.8 V typ, sourced from BIAS) already cover the\nlow-battery case, so an external line UVLO buys nothing.\nConsequences. (a) Pin 6 is high impedance with a ~5 uA hysteresis current source flowing OUT of it once above VUVLO. NOTHING on this\nsheet holds it low, so the EN_BOOST pulldown on mcu_can MUST exist -- 'floating = boost off' is only true if it is fitted. (b) ABSOLUTE\nMAXIMUM on pin 6 is 3.8 V to AGND (datasheet 8.1). A 3.3 V GPIO leaves 0.5 V of margin, so EN_BOOST must never see a 5 V pull-up.\nVUVLO(rising) is 1.5 V typ / 1.575 V max, so 3.3 V drives it hard enough. (c) Pin 6 is also the SYNC input; driving it DC means no\nexternal clock sync, which is intended."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.0 29.82 0)
		(size 103.19 16.8)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f0873e2d-e855-5560-ba12-119b3c0d21a2")
	)
